WEBVTT

00:17.315 --> 00:19.276
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you.

00:19.359 --> 00:20.193
Thank you.

00:20.277 --> 00:23.655
Up 'til now, I was confident I
could talk to pretty much anyone.

00:24.156 --> 00:25.157
Minato.

00:25.240 --> 00:26.908
- Minato.
- Minato.

00:26.992 --> 00:28.702
- But...
- Oh, Hikawa.

00:29.745 --> 00:31.288
Whenever I talk to her...

00:31.371 --> 00:32.956
I always feel so awkward.

00:33.457 --> 00:35.375
We just finished morning practice.

00:36.209 --> 00:38.128
Is there anything we can talk about?

00:38.754 --> 00:41.590
Oh, by the way, Igarashi was here
yesterday...

00:41.673 --> 00:42.758
Whoa, her face...

00:43.258 --> 00:44.968
Was that a sore subject?

00:46.219 --> 00:48.096
Yeah, they definitely don't seem close.

00:48.180 --> 00:50.557
And Igarashi came across as pretty
intense.

00:51.725 --> 00:53.101
Maybe she doesn't like him.

00:53.894 --> 00:54.895
I messed up.

00:55.395 --> 00:59.357
Maybe junior high was always off-limits
and I should've never even brought it up.

00:59.441 --> 01:00.901
Nice job, Minato.

01:01.943 --> 01:02.986
Oh, I'm sorry.

01:03.487 --> 01:05.906
We should just stop talking about
junior high.

01:07.491 --> 01:10.160
Jeez, could I have phrased that any
more awkwardly?

01:10.786 --> 01:12.913
Man, I'm really crashing and
burning here.

01:13.789 --> 01:16.792
The more I talk, the deeper I dig
myself into a hole.

01:17.751 --> 01:18.585
Wait...

01:19.169 --> 01:21.004
Have I always been like this?

01:27.344 --> 01:29.054
Ah, the cold air feels so good.

01:31.515 --> 01:33.934
- Koyun.
- Why do you have to be such a busybody?

01:37.187 --> 01:38.271
I don't get it.

01:39.481 --> 01:41.233
The sound of the door locking...

01:41.733 --> 01:42.818
It makes me sick.

01:44.653 --> 01:45.904
I think I heard it.

01:50.492 --> 01:52.244
Did Koyun just... Hold on.

01:52.744 --> 01:54.079
What just happened?

01:54.162 --> 01:56.206
Aw, man. I think...

01:56.706 --> 01:59.209
Don't try to put the moves on her
or be weird!

02:00.252 --> 02:01.795
Miki's totally gonna kill me.

02:04.381 --> 02:05.215
Huh?

03:37.140 --> 03:39.142
Change

03:41.019 --> 03:43.396
SCHOOL NURSE'S OFFICE

03:43.480 --> 03:45.941
- GLOOM
- Oh, come on!

03:46.691 --> 03:48.235
Are you just eating a sweet bun for lunch

03:48.318 --> 03:49.444
again?

03:49.986 --> 03:50.820
Noriko.

03:51.446 --> 03:54.157
Is there any way to keep yourself
from getting mad?

03:54.241 --> 03:55.617
Wow, I didn't think that you ever

03:55.700 --> 03:57.577
- got mad!
- It's so hot. It's so cold.

03:58.995 --> 04:00.038
Were you in a fight?

04:00.121 --> 04:01.164
Uh... Mm...

04:02.749 --> 04:03.583
Well...

04:03.667 --> 04:07.420
It's natural to get angry from time to
time, and it's important to not keep

04:07.504 --> 04:08.588
bottling it up.

04:09.089 --> 04:10.090
Hmm.

04:10.757 --> 04:14.427
I wish I could just take it out
on someone else to make me feel better.

04:14.511 --> 04:17.555
But I'm just not the type of person
who can do that.

04:18.473 --> 04:20.392
I know that much about myself.

04:21.851 --> 04:24.980
If anything, I just end up regretting
whatever I said.

04:25.063 --> 04:25.981
SELF-LOATHING

04:26.064 --> 04:27.232
You're a difficult one.

04:28.149 --> 04:31.361
I don't know what happened, but if
you're upset, it's best to communicate

04:31.444 --> 04:33.446
your feelings to the other person.

04:33.530 --> 04:35.865
If you don't like something, then just
say that.

04:35.949 --> 04:36.866
Communicate...

04:37.784 --> 04:38.660
I didn't do that.

04:39.619 --> 04:40.495
In that moment...

04:41.037 --> 04:42.747
I was just so upset...

04:43.540 --> 04:44.582
It makes me sick.

04:45.458 --> 04:46.918
I intentionally hurt him.

04:47.877 --> 04:52.090
And I did it without even hearing
Amamiya out or explaining myself.

04:53.300 --> 04:54.592
I'm still frustrated.

04:55.093 --> 04:58.346
And now pile onto it, the regret
over what I said to him.

05:01.725 --> 05:03.393
- I just want some peace and quiet.
- Sigh.

05:03.476 --> 05:06.021
Stop sounding like an old fart, and be a
teenager.

05:07.939 --> 05:08.857
Oh, there you are.

05:10.734 --> 05:11.568
Hey, Koyun.

05:12.068 --> 05:13.695
I'm gonna eat my lunch here too.

05:14.321 --> 05:16.573
I already told you, this isn't
a cafeteria.

05:17.073 --> 05:18.450
Do you want any of this?

05:18.533 --> 05:19.451
No, thanks.

05:19.534 --> 05:20.535
Seriously?

05:21.036 --> 05:22.746
Is something wrong?

05:22.829 --> 05:25.290
Just wanted to check in and see how
you were.

05:25.373 --> 05:26.333
This morning...

05:26.833 --> 05:28.376
I caught your conversation...

05:28.877 --> 05:30.170
with Minato.

05:30.253 --> 05:31.087
Ugh.

05:38.845 --> 05:41.431
Just clean up after yourselves before you
leave.

05:41.514 --> 05:43.224
- Okay.
- Okay.

05:44.642 --> 05:45.602
NURSE IS MAKING ROUNDS

05:45.685 --> 05:46.519
So, look, Koyun...

05:47.562 --> 05:49.064
Minato tends to...

05:51.524 --> 05:53.026
ego, is kinda childish, and can be

05:53.109 --> 05:53.401
Hey, w-wait a minute.

05:53.485 --> 05:54.319
Get too close, oversteps, has a big

05:54.402 --> 05:57.280
- ego, is kinda childish, and can be
- Hey, w-wait a minute.

05:57.364 --> 05:59.282
But he's not a bad guy, I promise you.

06:00.867 --> 06:03.161
And I hope this doesn't come across
weird...

06:03.244 --> 06:06.831
But Minato and I actually knew
of you since back in junior high.

06:07.457 --> 06:08.291
What?

06:09.125 --> 06:10.835
We didn't know your name...

06:11.336 --> 06:14.839
But the other day, when you said you
were on the basketball team, I put it

06:14.923 --> 06:16.966
- together.
- Basketball.

06:17.467 --> 06:19.677
- Does that mean...
- Mm-hm.

06:20.720 --> 06:22.514
Miki let us know what happened.

06:22.597 --> 06:25.350
She told us about how you were being
bullied back then.

06:28.561 --> 06:30.021
- Good morning, Koyun!
- Hm?

06:30.605 --> 06:33.775
I got here with time to spare, which
never happens so...

06:35.860 --> 06:36.694
Huh?

06:37.237 --> 06:39.155
What the... Who would...?

06:39.239 --> 06:40.573
Don't worry about it.

06:40.657 --> 06:42.700
What do you mean, "Don't worry about it?"

06:42.784 --> 06:43.785
How long has...?

06:43.868 --> 06:44.953
I can't remember.

06:45.453 --> 06:46.538
Since forever?

06:49.124 --> 06:51.000
I hope it all ends soon.

06:52.669 --> 06:55.547
So Miki told you guys what happened
back then.

06:55.630 --> 06:57.382
Yeah, but don't get mad at her.

06:57.882 --> 07:01.136
It was just because she was
really worried about you at the time.

07:01.219 --> 07:02.929
Yeah... I know.

07:03.012 --> 07:04.389
Miki also said...

07:05.098 --> 07:07.475
She didn't realize her friend was
struggling.

07:07.976 --> 07:10.270
And that she had no idea how to help you.

07:10.770 --> 07:14.023
I wondered why she never told me about
what was going on.

07:14.107 --> 07:17.485
Maybe she felt as though she couldn't
trust me.

07:18.153 --> 07:20.113
It all just makes me so sad.

07:20.655 --> 07:21.906
You're not untrustworthy.

07:21.990 --> 07:24.826
Maybe she just didn't wanna bother
you or worry you.

07:24.909 --> 07:26.453
And nothing more than that.

07:27.162 --> 07:29.372
Do you really think that's what it is?

07:29.456 --> 07:30.457
UGH, UGH, UGH

07:30.540 --> 07:31.833
I don't want her holding back just to
spare my feelings.

07:31.916 --> 07:33.209
Whoa, hey, calm down.

07:34.169 --> 07:37.213
- So. yeah...
- I had no idea she felt that way.

07:38.548 --> 07:40.592
The reason I didn't talk to her about it...

07:40.675 --> 07:42.135
Go for it, Miki!

07:43.887 --> 07:45.972
- Nice!
- That was awesome!

07:46.055 --> 07:48.892
Was because she was so dedicated to
her club activities.

07:48.975 --> 07:54.063
Whereas I only kept showing up to them
because I was too afraid to quit.

07:54.606 --> 07:55.732
We were opposites.

07:56.900 --> 07:57.734
So, no.

07:57.817 --> 08:00.987
I never though she was unreliable
or that I couldn't trust her.

08:02.697 --> 08:03.531
Hmm.

08:04.574 --> 08:08.244
And seeing how you and Miki interact,
I guess Minato might've also picked

08:08.328 --> 08:09.162
up on it by now.

08:09.245 --> 08:12.207
That you and her were old friends from
the basketball team.

08:12.290 --> 08:13.124
Oh.

08:13.208 --> 08:15.919
So that's probably why Minato was
concerned about you.

08:16.002 --> 08:16.836
That's all.

08:17.795 --> 08:18.630
That's why.

08:19.339 --> 08:21.090
Oh... I'm sorry.

08:21.633 --> 08:23.551
Let's stop talking about junior high.

08:24.511 --> 08:26.554
That's why Amamiya said what he said.

08:27.972 --> 08:31.434
And I completely took it the wrong
way and said all those awful things to

08:31.518 --> 08:32.352
him.

08:33.394 --> 08:35.063
H-How embarrassing.

08:35.146 --> 08:36.064
Are you okay?

08:37.106 --> 08:39.984
Not at all.
I must offer an apology right away.

08:40.485 --> 08:42.654
That sounds so... uh, formal.

08:43.238 --> 08:44.906
Want me to just tell him for you?

08:44.989 --> 08:45.949
No.

08:46.032 --> 08:47.742
I must express the apology.

08:47.825 --> 08:48.826
What?

08:49.869 --> 08:52.705
I'm telling you, it probably didn't
bother him at all.

08:53.206 --> 08:54.415
It's fine, don't worry.

08:54.499 --> 08:55.708
It's Minato.

08:56.793 --> 08:58.294
Hey, Amamiya!

09:00.213 --> 09:01.548
Hey, sorry, my bad.

09:01.631 --> 09:02.465
Over here!

09:04.259 --> 09:06.302
Hey. Hey, d'you hear me?

09:06.386 --> 09:08.638
Whoa! Yo, what's up?

09:09.347 --> 09:11.099
Are you mad or s- something?

09:12.267 --> 09:14.143
Sorry, I wasn't paying attention.

09:14.227 --> 09:15.395
Uh. Oh.

09:16.521 --> 09:17.605
Dude, you scared me.

09:17.689 --> 09:19.399
I thought you were mad at me.

09:19.482 --> 09:23.069
No, dummy, he just looks intense
when he's not smiling.

09:25.822 --> 09:28.074
Why do you have to be such a busybody?

09:28.908 --> 09:33.121
Was she upset because I talked to
Igarashi or something?

09:33.955 --> 09:36.749
And why would that make her so mad?

09:37.750 --> 09:39.377
- You shouldn't do to others what you
- Nice!

09:39.460 --> 09:40.920
- Wouldn't want done to yourself, I know
- Good arm!

09:41.004 --> 09:42.046
- That.
- Thanks.

09:42.130 --> 09:44.465
- But I shouldn't do the opposite?
- My turn!

09:44.549 --> 09:46.175
- Oops.
- I don't get it.

09:47.093 --> 09:47.927
Maybe...

09:48.845 --> 09:50.263
We're just too different.

09:50.763 --> 09:52.724
In our values and ways of thinking.

09:54.475 --> 09:56.144
What might work for me...

09:57.895 --> 09:59.814
Seems to not work for her.

10:01.107 --> 10:04.027
So whatever I do, it only ends up
bothering her.

10:07.238 --> 10:11.242
Is it arrogant of me to think I should do
something for her in the first place?

10:11.326 --> 10:12.452
Is that it, Miki?

10:12.535 --> 10:13.536
Huh?

10:14.412 --> 10:17.248
But, if I'm arrogant, couldn't you
say the same for her?

10:17.874 --> 10:21.377
She draws a line between people she
likes and people she doesn't.

10:21.461 --> 10:24.464
Yota and Miki are on the side of the
people she accepts.

10:24.547 --> 10:27.050
On the other hand, I'm on the side she
writes off.

10:28.676 --> 10:29.510
UNEASY

10:29.594 --> 10:31.804
- Man, it's starting to make me angry.
- Whoa!

10:34.349 --> 10:35.933
Whoa! What's wrong?

10:36.517 --> 10:38.728
Yeah. I'll stop getting involved with her.

10:39.228 --> 10:41.189
It's not doing either of us any good.

10:41.272 --> 10:43.691
So, I won't worry about it anymore.

10:44.984 --> 10:47.862
Yota.
Where were you during the lunch break?

10:48.363 --> 10:49.572
Mmm.

10:50.239 --> 10:51.240
The bathroom?

10:51.324 --> 10:52.325
Forever.

10:56.371 --> 11:00.041
School's over now, but I never found
a good time to apologize.

11:01.042 --> 11:03.878
Is there ever really a good time
to apologize?

11:03.961 --> 11:05.088
APOLOGIZE TIMING

11:05.588 --> 11:09.175
Well, let's hope I get a chance tomorrow.

11:09.258 --> 11:10.301
See you, Minato.

11:11.094 --> 11:11.928
See ya.

11:13.846 --> 11:14.931
Oh, I, um, I mean...

11:30.947 --> 11:35.034
I'm realizing, up until now, I never made
the effort to see him for who he really

11:35.118 --> 11:35.952
is.

11:39.580 --> 11:41.791
I assumed he'd treat me like others have.

11:41.874 --> 11:44.335
So I wrote him off, just like that.

11:45.378 --> 11:47.338
Rejected him without even knowing him.

11:48.131 --> 11:52.093
I've been doing things to him that
I know I wouldn't want done to me.

11:58.891 --> 12:00.101
That face again.

12:00.727 --> 12:03.730
The one she makes around people she
keeps her guard up with.

12:04.814 --> 12:07.692
I thought maybe we could eventually
become friends.

12:08.443 --> 12:10.611
I guess that was just my ego talking.

12:11.487 --> 12:12.655
I was doing it for me.

12:13.322 --> 12:15.074
And to her, I was just annoying.

12:15.825 --> 12:18.703
Maybe it would've been better if I
hadn't gotten involved with her in the

12:18.786 --> 12:20.246
- first place.
- Amamiya!

12:21.164 --> 12:21.998
Huh?

12:24.792 --> 12:25.626
I'm sorry.

12:28.713 --> 12:31.716
I'm sorry, but can you and I... talk?

12:37.388 --> 12:38.222
Um...

12:38.806 --> 12:40.224
Do you have time right now?

12:40.725 --> 12:41.684
Yeah.

12:41.768 --> 12:43.936
My club doesn't start for a few minutes.

12:45.646 --> 12:47.523
So, about this morning...

12:48.399 --> 12:49.317
What should I do?

12:50.026 --> 12:51.235
This is so embarrassing.

12:51.778 --> 12:53.321
Everything about this is embarrassing.

12:53.404 --> 12:55.072
MISUNDERSTANDING, PARANOIA
SELF-CONSCIOUSNES

12:55.156 --> 12:55.990
Ugh.

12:56.574 --> 12:58.743
I'm sorry for saying such mean things.

12:59.535 --> 13:00.369
Sure.

13:00.453 --> 13:04.040
In the moment, I wondered why you knew
about something from when I was

13:04.123 --> 13:06.125
in junior high.

13:06.709 --> 13:10.296
I just couldn't stand the thought that
you might've heard about it from

13:10.379 --> 13:11.380
Igarashi.

13:11.881 --> 13:12.799
DOESN'T GET PERSONAL SPACE
ONLY WANTS TO HELP

13:12.882 --> 13:16.385
But, Yota told me at lunch that it was
just a misunderstanding.

13:17.094 --> 13:18.012
Yota did?

13:18.596 --> 13:19.430
Wait.

13:20.139 --> 13:20.973
Mmm.

13:21.849 --> 13:23.768
- The bathroom?
- That liar.

13:24.852 --> 13:25.770
I'm sorry, I...

13:26.729 --> 13:28.481
I misunderstood things.

13:29.232 --> 13:30.191
And I was rude.

13:30.817 --> 13:31.651
And I...

13:32.944 --> 13:33.778
I, uh...

13:34.612 --> 13:35.488
I have...

13:35.571 --> 13:37.573
I have so much I want to say.

13:38.950 --> 13:39.784
But I can never get it to come out

13:39.867 --> 13:40.701
WANT TO APOLOGIZE PROPERLY FOR WHOSE SAKE?

13:40.785 --> 13:41.661
how I want it to.

13:41.744 --> 13:42.787
SELF-SATISFACTION?
WANT TO CHANGE

13:42.870 --> 13:46.749
The more my thoughts start to pile up on
me, the more everything I try to say

13:46.833 --> 13:49.794
gets stuck in my throat.

13:51.671 --> 13:54.382
All the feelings I can't voice try to
escape as tears.

13:58.177 --> 13:59.011
Oh no!

13:59.554 --> 14:00.429
No, no, no, no!

14:00.513 --> 14:01.556
Get back in there!

14:02.056 --> 14:03.266
Oh, this always happens.

14:03.349 --> 14:05.184
The apologizer can't cry!

14:05.268 --> 14:06.477
Dry up, dry up, dry up!

14:07.144 --> 14:09.272
Hikawa.

14:09.981 --> 14:11.274
Hey, it's okay.

14:12.733 --> 14:14.861
You don't have to apologize so much.

14:14.944 --> 14:17.363
Look, if anything, I'm the one
who made you feel bad.

14:17.446 --> 14:19.949
Wait, hold on. I was just pissed
off at her a moment ago. Why am I

14:20.032 --> 14:20.867
trying to comfort her all of a sudden?

14:20.950 --> 14:23.077
Seriously, you can say whatever you
want to me, alright?

14:23.160 --> 14:24.370
Don't bottle it up. Huh?

14:25.246 --> 14:26.789
DRIP

14:27.498 --> 14:28.332
Uh?

14:28.916 --> 14:32.545
When someone's kind to me when I'm
holding my tears back, the floodgates

14:32.628 --> 14:33.671
just open and...

14:35.715 --> 14:37.216
- Oh.
- Tears?

14:39.969 --> 14:41.220
LINT, LOOSE THREADS

14:41.304 --> 14:42.263
SLIP

14:42.972 --> 14:43.806
- You know,
- Hm?

14:44.640 --> 14:48.019
I was lying when I said I didn't know
Igarashi.

14:48.603 --> 14:49.854
- Huh?
- It's the opposite.

14:51.731 --> 14:53.941
We're actually not on very good terms.

14:55.902 --> 14:57.528
Where are we taking this again?

14:58.154 --> 15:00.072
Turn left here and go straight.

15:02.408 --> 15:03.534
Tears, just the two of us...

15:03.618 --> 15:04.994
They'll get the wrong idea!

15:05.912 --> 15:06.746
Hikawa...

15:09.665 --> 15:11.792
- It's so heavy, right?
- Huh?

15:11.876 --> 15:13.336
Look at this. Look.

15:13.419 --> 15:14.337
What do you think?

15:14.879 --> 15:16.756
- Hm?
- What're they doing?

15:16.839 --> 15:19.383
Maybe they caught a rare monster
or something?

15:19.467 --> 15:21.302
Oh, my parents are really into that game.

15:21.385 --> 15:24.847
They like that you have to walk around
doing it, so you get exercise.

15:27.224 --> 15:28.309
Thank you for that.

15:31.520 --> 15:33.814
- What's that?
- Uh... Oh, um, that's...

15:34.815 --> 15:36.192
My Pomeranian.

15:38.319 --> 15:39.403
Oh, I made her laugh.

15:42.031 --> 15:43.074
It's so cute.

15:48.079 --> 15:49.330
I should get going now.

15:49.830 --> 15:50.748
Oh, sorry.

15:51.248 --> 15:52.249
Well...

15:55.294 --> 15:56.754
I'll see ya tomorrow.

15:57.296 --> 15:58.130
Yeah.

15:59.006 --> 15:59.840
See ya then.

16:15.147 --> 16:17.775
Hmm? Wait, now that I think about it...

16:18.275 --> 16:21.195
Hikawa said she and Igarashi are on bad
terms.

16:21.696 --> 16:23.239
But when I asked him...

16:23.906 --> 16:28.035
Oh, by the way, Igarashi, do you remember
Hikawa?

16:30.371 --> 16:31.205
Huh?

16:32.039 --> 16:32.915
Hikawa?

16:33.791 --> 16:36.502
Nah, there was no one by that name in our
junior high.

16:37.336 --> 16:38.170
So he said.

16:39.130 --> 16:40.548
What's going on there?

16:41.549 --> 16:42.383
Hmmm...

16:47.722 --> 16:49.557
Neither of them seem to be lying.

16:50.057 --> 16:51.142
It's the opposite.

16:51.642 --> 16:52.518
Wait, who?

16:53.019 --> 16:55.229
What happened between those two
in the past?

16:55.312 --> 16:57.648
Why do you have to be such a busybody?

16:57.732 --> 16:58.566
Ugh!

16:59.817 --> 17:00.651
Huh...

17:01.485 --> 17:03.320
Is something wrong, Amamiya?

17:03.404 --> 17:04.405
What?

17:04.488 --> 17:06.699
- No, nothing.
- Don't lie!

17:06.782 --> 17:10.369
You haven't been listening to a single
word I've been saying, have you?

17:14.206 --> 17:16.876
- What are you, his girlfriend?
- Or you sound like one.

17:16.959 --> 17:19.545
Minato, if you keep spacing out,
your noodles will get all soggy.

17:19.628 --> 17:21.964
What kind of combination is that, man?

17:22.048 --> 17:22.882
That's gross.

17:23.424 --> 17:24.300
They're delicious.

17:24.383 --> 17:25.801
Too many carbs.

17:25.885 --> 17:27.553
- Huh?
- Yota.

17:28.137 --> 17:30.681
Yota told me that it was a
misunderstanding.

17:31.640 --> 17:34.268
Yota... She calls him by his first name.

17:35.019 --> 17:39.523
The exams are over, and winter break is
starting, so I'll lose any common ground.

17:45.154 --> 17:46.530
SLURRRP

17:46.614 --> 17:47.990
You possessed or something?

17:48.074 --> 17:48.949
So what?

17:51.410 --> 17:55.206
If I talk to her the next time I see her,
I wonder how she'll react.

17:56.040 --> 18:00.878
Will it be awkward for her, or will
she keep her distance like she used to?

18:00.961 --> 18:01.962
Hmm.

18:02.630 --> 18:03.589
I don't know...

18:04.381 --> 18:05.216
Hm?

18:06.675 --> 18:07.510
Oh.

18:07.593 --> 18:08.552
THUMP

18:09.303 --> 18:11.472
Uh, hey, uh, Amamiya.

18:14.141 --> 18:16.477
Oh, um, well, I, uh...

18:17.353 --> 18:18.187
Hm?

18:19.188 --> 18:21.065
Um, about yesterday.

18:22.108 --> 18:24.318
I'm sorry for crying when I was
apologizing.

18:25.152 --> 18:26.570
It was so embarrassing.

18:27.947 --> 18:29.281
STUNNED

18:29.365 --> 18:32.243
And I promise, I didn't just cry
because I thought it'd make you

18:32.326 --> 18:33.828
- forgive me or something.
- No.

18:33.911 --> 18:34.745
Huh?

18:35.246 --> 18:38.332
No problem.
Sometimes people just get overwhelmed.

18:38.415 --> 18:40.459
There doesn't have to be a particular
reason.

18:40.543 --> 18:42.002
No need to explain yourself.

18:42.086 --> 18:43.045
Huh?

18:43.129 --> 18:44.338
Does that happen to you?

18:44.421 --> 18:45.256
BLANK STARE

18:46.882 --> 18:48.467
- Of course.
- Huh?

18:48.551 --> 18:51.262
You think I don't get or express human
emotions?

18:51.345 --> 18:52.304
Oops.

18:52.805 --> 18:55.599
Aw, that's so mean! Sniffle, sniffle, sniffle.

18:55.683 --> 18:56.934
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

18:57.017 --> 18:58.144
I am surprised though.

18:58.227 --> 18:59.103
Oh.

18:59.603 --> 19:02.857
Listen, I know I may not look like it,
but I'm just a big softie.

19:04.900 --> 19:05.734
Hmmm...

19:06.527 --> 19:07.653
What's with that look?

19:12.449 --> 19:13.993
That's so mean.

19:18.956 --> 19:20.916
Well, I'm heading that way.

19:21.417 --> 19:22.960
Oh, club stuff?

19:23.043 --> 19:24.044
Yeah.

19:25.212 --> 19:26.046
Good luck then.

19:27.715 --> 19:28.591
Thanks.

19:37.016 --> 19:37.850
Ahhhh.

19:40.186 --> 19:41.187
Wahhhhh!

19:43.355 --> 19:46.192
I think I'm learning to stop assuming so
much.

19:46.275 --> 19:49.778
Like that people won't understand me
or that they'll reject me.

19:51.071 --> 19:51.906
Huh?

19:53.365 --> 19:55.576
Come to my work during winter break! Kay,
thanks!

19:55.659 --> 19:57.912
It feels like something has changed a
little.

19:58.913 --> 19:59.997
Or maybe nothing has.

20:00.080 --> 20:00.998
I'LL TELL YOTA TOO

20:01.874 --> 20:02.958
Too soon to tell.

20:04.168 --> 20:07.296
All I know is winter break starts
tomorrow.

21:39.096 --> 21:42.016
KAWAII CAFÉ, WELCOME, WINTER BREAK FAIR PERIOD: DEC. 24TH THROUGH JAN. 10TH

21:42.099 --> 21:43.517
Miharu! Sora! Been too long!

21:44.977 --> 21:47.021
- Yay!
- Yay!

21:47.104 --> 21:49.565
- So how've you been?
- Haven't seen you guys since graduation.

21:49.648 --> 21:50.482
MEETING UP WITH JR. HIGH FRIENDS FOR THE FIRST TIME IN A WHILE

21:50.566 --> 21:52.359
How's high school going?

21:52.443 --> 21:53.736
It's been nice and quiet.

21:54.236 --> 21:55.070
Tell me...

21:55.571 --> 21:57.072
You got boyfriends yet?

21:57.156 --> 21:58.032
No way.

21:58.115 --> 21:59.283
Yeah, same here.

21:59.366 --> 22:00.367
Wow, no hesitation.

22:00.993 --> 22:02.036
I'm so surprised, Miki.

22:02.119 --> 22:04.246
You dated a lot back in junior high.

22:04.330 --> 22:07.333
Like that hot upperclassman and the
volleyball player from another school.

22:07.416 --> 22:08.250
Ugh!

22:09.752 --> 22:13.630
Guys would just come on strong
and confess their feelings...

22:13.714 --> 22:15.466
AN UPPERCLASSMAN WITH NO CONNECTION

22:17.926 --> 22:18.761
we'd start dating.

22:18.844 --> 22:21.096
Then, later, they'd break up with me,
saying I wasn't the person that

22:21.180 --> 22:22.765
they thought I was. Every time.

22:24.016 --> 22:24.850
Grr!

22:24.933 --> 22:28.062
Like, don't fantasize about who
you think I am, then get mad when I

22:28.145 --> 22:29.146
don't live up to it.

22:29.229 --> 22:31.148
Whoa, she switched to gorilla mode.

22:31.231 --> 22:32.441
Sorry I mentioned it.

22:33.192 --> 22:36.528
So I guess in the end I really can't
technically say I dated them.

22:37.363 --> 22:40.449
I promise you, though, the next
time I date someone, I wanna be

22:40.532 --> 22:46.080
the one to confess my feelings to
the person I like before we start dating.

22:46.163 --> 22:48.457
- Anyone in mind?
- Nobody.

22:49.750 --> 22:50.876
What about Amamiya?

22:51.418 --> 22:54.296
I guess things would get awkward
if I asked that now.

22:54.838 --> 22:56.006
- And you, Koyuki?
- Huh?

22:56.090 --> 22:57.299
Do you have a boyfriend?

22:59.176 --> 23:00.010
A boyfriend?

23:04.264 --> 23:05.265
Don't need one.

23:06.600 --> 23:09.603
Plus I don't really think I can
handle dating, to be honest.

23:10.604 --> 23:13.565
So I think it's amazing that you two
have been with your boyfriends

23:13.649 --> 23:14.483
for so long.

23:15.818 --> 23:17.486
Ah, it's not that big a deal.

23:18.404 --> 23:20.280
Do you have any pictures or anything?

23:21.532 --> 23:22.366
Sure, wanna see?

23:24.368 --> 23:26.412
Well, I gotta head to work now.

23:26.495 --> 23:27.496
See ya!

23:27.579 --> 23:29.373
- Bye-bye!
- Let's hang again soon.

23:31.417 --> 23:32.876
- I think she's making things more
- Hm?

23:32.960 --> 23:34.545
Complicated than they are.

23:34.628 --> 23:38.132
Well, don't forget about that whole
Igarashi thing.

23:39.049 --> 23:42.636
Yeah, but to be completely honest,
I've never really understood why she

23:42.719 --> 23:46.014
ever dated him in the first place.

23:47.182 --> 23:48.892
Like, I thought she hated his guts.

23:48.976 --> 23:50.394
Oh my gosh, right?! So I'm not the

23:50.477 --> 23:52.479
- only one who didn't get it!
- That whole thing...

23:52.563 --> 23:54.189
Was probably my fault.
